{{Quote|There are so many ways to die in this galaxy&hellip;and a song for each one. But today, I will play a new song. A song of ''life''.|Max Rebo, to Garsa Fwip|<ref name="Max Rebo 1">[[Return of the Jedi – Max Rebo 1|''Return of the Jedi – Max Rebo'' 1]]</ref>}}
'''Maximilian "Max" Rebo''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Ortolan]] from [[Orto]] and a popular [[Jizz-wailer]] musician who led the [[Max Rebo Band]]. He mainly played the [[red ball jett organ]], which he played with his [[Limb|feet]]; he and his band often performed for criminals and gangsters.

==Biography==
===Early life===
Maximilian Rebo<ref name="Fancy Man" /> was [[Reproduction|born]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> on the [[Temperature|cold]] [[planet]]<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> of [[Orto]]. At some point Rebo formed a [[band]], called the [[Max Rebo Band]], which would go on to perform<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> [[Jizz]]-style [[music]]<ref name="RotJ novelas">[[Star Wars: Return of the Jedi (paperback novel)|''Star Wars: Return of the Jedi'' junior novelization]]</ref> for [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> Rebo also had a brother named [[Azool Phantelle]].<ref name="Blue Brothers" />

===Mistaken identity===
{{Quote|We're doomed! Jabba will surely throw us to the sarlacc when he finds my brother has been stealing on his turf!|Max Rebo, to Azool Phantelle|<ref name="Blue Brothers" />}}
[[File:Azool_and_Max.png|thumb|left|208x208px|Rebo and Azool make their escape from the pursuers.]]
At some point, Azool swindled several of the inhabitants of the [[spaceport]] [[Mos Eisley]] on the planet [[Tatooine]]. The victims mistook Rebo for Azool and began chasing the musician. Rebo then collided with two Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s while fleeing toward [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]]. Before the [[trooper]]s could punish him for the collision, Azool spotted Rebo while passing on a [[speeder bike]] and pulled his brother out of harm's way and onto the bike.<ref name="Blue Brothers" />

As the pair sped away from the angry stormtroopers and locals, Rebo admonished Azool for his life of crime. He fretted that Jabba the Hutt, who employed Rebo, would punish both brothers for Azool's crimes, as they had taken place within the crime [[lord]]'s [[Jabba's criminal empire|territory]]. Unconcerned, Azool avoided a [[missile]] fired by [[Boushh]], but then Rebo stopped the chase by grabbing Azool's bag of stolen [[Currency|funds]] and throwing the contents out to those chasing them. Rebo and Azool then got out of the speeder, with Azool saddened when he watched his funds being taken away by the pursuers. Jabba the Hutt then came to both of them, asking Rebo what had occurred. Rebo gave the excuse that Azool had been causing trouble on Jabba's territory, and Azool claimed he had not known that it was Jabba's territory. As a result, Jabba punished Azool by forcing him to be a [[waiter]] on the ''[[Khetanna]]''.<ref name="Blue Brothers" />

===Performing for Jabba===
[[File:HoorayForEvil.png|thumb|right|275px|Max Rebo (right) performing for Jabba the Hutt]]
In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> Rebo and his band performed for Jabba. While performing, they were interrupted by the scream of Jabba's [[Slavery|slave]] dancer [[Oola]] as she was dropped into the Hutt's [[rancor]] pit below his throne room for defying him which interrupted the band's performance. Later, the band was present when [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] entered the palace disguised as the [[bounty hunter]] Boushh. At night, several members of the band accompanied Jabba into hiding as Organa freed the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]] from [[carbonite]].<ref name="Episode VI" />

===The second plot to kill Jabba===
Max Rebo then traveled aboard Jabba's [[sail barge]], the ''[[Khetanna]]'', to the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]], where Solo was to be executed.<ref name="Episode VI" /> After [[Daladit-Chan]] gave a message to his son, [[Umpass-stay]], to [[Death|kill]] Jabba, Rebo had to carry out the task to kill Jabba, using some sort of [[poison]]. Max got caught, but got lucky when [[Luke Skywalker]] busted into the [[sail barge]], and distracted Jabba. At the end of the [[Standard day|day]], Max Rebo was alive.<ref name="Max Rebo 1">[[Return of the Jedi – Max Rebo 1|''Return of the Jedi – Max Rebo'' 1]]</ref> The ''Khetanna'' was [[Rescue of Han Solo|destroyed]] by Solo and his associates, however, causing the sail barge to explode in [[Fire|flame]] all over the [[desert]].<ref name="Episode VI" /> However, Rebo was able to escape the destruction.<ref name="FACPOV Insider">{{InsiderCite|218|A Certain Point of View}}</ref>

===New Republic, new gig===
[[File:Max_Rebo_at_the_Sanctuary.png|thumb|left|275px|Rebo played at the Sanctuary in Mos Espa during the New Republic Era.]]
By [[9 ABY]],<ref name="BOBF Date">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> the Ortolan came to work in [[Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary]], the [[cantina]] operated by the [[Twi'lek]] [[Garsa Fwip]] during the [[New Republic Era]]. At the Sanctuary, Rebo continued to play the red ball jet organ (albeit a new model),<ref name="Chapter 1" /> and was performing when the cantina was visited by the former [[bounty hunter]] and [[Daimyo]] of Mos Espa [[Boba Fett]] on multiple occasions.<ref name="Chapter 1" /><ref name="Chapter 2">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}}</ref> Rebo was accompanied by a [[Unidentified Bith musician (Sanctuary)|Bith musician]] on [[guitar]] and astromech [[R0-1N6]] on the drums.<ref name="Chapter 2" /> The [[Pyke Syndicate]] later [[Destruction of Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|bombed]] the Sanctuary during business hours; Fwip and the band were killed in the blast,<ref name="Chapter 6">{{BOBF|Chapter 6: From the Desert Comes a Stranger}}</ref> but Rebo once again survived an explosive experience.<ref name="Insider 224">{{InsiderCite|224|Hit it, Max!}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Originally, I was given a character called '6-Eye,' who was a sluglike character with six red eyes and six arms; it was eventually cut from the production. So, then Phil Tippett took me to the creature room, which was up some stairs on the side of the studio and said, 'Oh, there's another puppet you can play that you might quite like. And there, before me, was this bright blue vision of loveliness. And I thought, 'Yes, I must play him.'"|Simon Williamson, on how he got the Max Rebo part|<ref name="Insider 224" />}}
Max Rebo first appeared in the [[1983]] ''[[Star Wars]]'' film, [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="Episode VI" /> While at times described as such, Rebo was not a puppet but instead a costume; performer [[Simon Williamson]] needed to sit within the suit to play the character. Williamson got the part after the character he was originally set to play, [[Sic-Six]], was cut from the film. Shown the Rebo costume as an alternative part he could claim by [[Phil Tippett]], Williamson described seeing Rebo as a "blue vision of loveliness" and felt a great need to play him.<ref name="Insider 224" /> The [[2016]] young reader's [[Canon]] reference book ''[[The Amazing Book of Star Wars]]'' misspells his last name as "Reebo."<ref name="AmazingBook">''[[The Amazing Book of Star Wars]]''</ref>

Rebo's design in the non-canon [[2022]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga]]'' re-uses<ref name="LEGOTSS">''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga]]''</ref> the design for his minifigure in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]]-era ''[[LEGO Classic Star Wars]]'' set [[w:c:brickipedia:75020 Jabba's Sail Barge|75020 Jabba's Sail Barge]].<ref name="LEGOSailBarge">{{LEGOCite|num=75020|name=Jabba's Sail Barge}}</ref> As a result, the character is depicted with a pair of arms instead of only legs, in line with [[Ortolan/Legends|Ortolans]] from the Legends continuity, as opposed to Canon Ortolans which possess only legs.

